cing are available yet, so the forecast rests almost entirely on the state's partisan lean. The seat is open with a term-limited president, which removes any incumbency effect in either direction.\n\nSome signs point to a somewhat friendlier national climate for Democrats: a September Tennessee poll found the president's approval underwater, and Democratic governors have invested in Tennessee House races. But the state has drifted further right in recent cycles, and a midterm-sized shift would need to be unusually large to put Tennessee in play. The Republican nominee is clearly favored, though the wide uncertainty reflects the absence of direct polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0603, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.11, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1055, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0961, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1038, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0969, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1086, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.082, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0965, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1008, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0993, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1057, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.104, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0893, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.08, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0958, "margin": -14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.104, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.0954, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.1047, "margin": -14.